commit(n,t,ds,ch,items,'The sheet associates a k-additive functor F_X to a simplicial object and identifies its values on the displayed C objects with nondegenerate cochains. It then studies maps from F_X to the functor of a simplex through a double-dual comparison. The written inclusion C^i(X_*) subset k^(X_[i]) is essential: H’s equality would erase the nondegeneracy condition. The example writes Mon, not Hom!, confirmed from the tall M and consistent with the exterior-power model; no replacement by a mathematically preferred notation was made. The main square explicitly qualifies the double-dual map by iso si X_n fini. For a finite set, the free module has a finite basis and evaluation into its double dual is an isomorphism; this limited fact was checked, not the entire functor-classification claim. The underbrace ticks and linking ticks are vertical equality signs, not quotation marks. A crossed F(X_*) attempt and a lowered X_* replacement in the main square are restored. The exact membership-like relation before G and the pale words on a remain uncertain. Foot number 340.',hand=['Paired short vertical ticks connect identified objects (k[X_*] to lambda_*, and cochains to their named complexes); they serve as vertical equals, not prose quotation marks. Their placement is confirmed at the repeated occurrences on this sheet.','Mon begins with a tall two-stem M; Hom! has a different initial H and raised exclamation on the preceding sheet. H confused the two here.','A narrow u can resemble n: the central mapping is u maps to F(u), twice with an open cup shape.','The pale on a has only partial low strokes; a grammatical expectation is not enough to remove its doubt.'],notation=[('C_* versus C_bullet','Starred simplicial chain object and its bullet complex; retained as written in the lambda identifications.'),('vertical equals','Two straight ticks linking vertically stacked identifications; rendered Vert.'),('double vee','Two separate vee strokes indicate the double dual; the finiteness qualification is explicit.')],abbr=[('k-add','k-additif'),('non dég','non dégénérées'),('gén','généralement'),('comm.','commutatif'),('R.','remarque')],checks=[check('339-text-functor','Functor determination and cochain identifications carried as source assertions; no proof of the full equivalence supplied.'),check('339-finite-double-dual','For a finite basis e_j of k[S], the dual coordinate basis gives evaluation e_j -> e_j** as a basis isomorphism; verifies only the finite-set label in the main square.','targeted proof check')],unresolved=[r'membership-like ni|in before G',r'pale on a',r'cancelled Hom in category fragment and cancelled lower marginal formula'])
